      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "🎧 > “Let's look at how the Inca built roads across the Andes. They had no wheels or horses, so the roads were designed for people and llamas. On steep slopes, they built stairs cut into the rock. To cross deep valleys, they made bridges from woven grass, which had to be replaced every year. Along the roads, there were small stations where messengers could rest. Amazingly, a message could travel about two hundred and forty kilometres in a single day.”"
          }
